      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/research/slt/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-slt&#34;&gt;What is SLT?&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#what-is-slt&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Singular Learning Theory (SLT) is a mathematical framework developed by Sumio Watanabe for analyzing statistical learning when the model is singular (non-regular).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;key-concepts&#34;&gt;Key Concepts&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#key-concepts&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RLCT (Real Log Canonical Threshold)&lt;/strong&gt;: A key quantity that determines generalization error&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Free Energy&lt;/strong&gt;: Measures model complexity in Bayesian inference&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Singular Models&lt;/strong&gt;: Models where the Fisher information matrix is degenerate&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;references&#34;&gt;References&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#references&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Watanabe, S. (2009). Algebraic Geometry and Statistical Learning Theory&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Watanabe, S. (2018). Mathematical Theory of Bayesian Statistics&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
